  "reason": "S480 (s480-boot-cheap-wins — `x is .V` built in the bootstrap): the §66 twin is graded on every Error it emits (twin-extra-error). Its `${ if (role is .Admin) { <p id=\"p\">admin</> } }` puts markup in a body-top `${ }` as a statement, which the bootstrap refuses by the SPEC's own rule — §17.6.10.1 E-MARKUP-STATEMENT-NOT-RENDERED (\"markup stands as a statement and no `lift` names it\"; §17.3: a body-top `${ … }` is evaluated, not rendered). Until `is .V` was built the twin stopped at the named refusal (UNSUPPORTED) and never reached that rule. The `is` half is the case's contract and holds: `role` is the enum `Role`, so neither §18.17 code fires. The legacy contract (no E-TYPE-062 on impl#1) is unchanged."
